# Datasets are re-downloadable with src/prepare_data.py and are NOT redistributed here.
# CIFAR-10's official page states no licence, so the images stay out of the public repository.
# The contents (not the directory) are excluded so that splits.json can be re-included below --
# git cannot un-ignore a file whose parent directory is itself ignored.
/data/*
!/data/splits.json

# Model checkpoints (~1.8 GB) and the derived evaluation cache are regenerable, so they stay out.
/runs/
*.pt
!**/.gitkeep
analysis/test_predictions.npz

# The published site's binaries. `main` carries source only; the `gh-pages` branch carries the two
# ONNX graphs (114 MB), the onnxruntime-web wasm (33 MB) and the 10,000 test thumbnails (23 MB).
# src/package_pages.py assembles that branch from a working copy of webapp/, so nothing here needs
# to be fetched by hand. Largest single file 57.8 MB, inside GitHub's 100 MB per-file cap.
*.onnx
/webapp/ort/
/webapp/data/test/

# Raw web pages fetched by the literature-search subagents (third-party content, ~35 MB).
/research_records/retrieval_cache/

# Source files of the reference implementations, read only to recover the mathematics.  The
# consulted repository declares no licence, so these stay as audit evidence and are not published.
/research_records/reference_consulted/

# Third-party paper PDFs and the course materials supplied by the unit are not part of the
# source code being published. Assignment 1's repository made the same choice.
*.pdf
*.pptx
*.docx

# The bilingual dialogue archive is evidence for the report appendix, not for the public
# repository. Assignment 1 kept it local for the same reason.
research_records/conversation_log.md

# Python and tooling noise.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local editor state.
.vscode/
.idea/

# Build output for the gh-pages branch; the branch itself is committed separately.
/pages_build/
